[2026-08-08 18:05:00] ARCHITECT: Phase-1 weakness acknowledged: every candidate was measured against the EMPTY baseline, so cycles did not chain. Phase 2 measures every candidate against the CURRENT INCUMBENT (active=["uncertainty_planning"]). Design constraints from env code: the ONLY hook sites reachable by a new mechanism without touching the inviolable env/runner files are (a) before_eval (repoops per-bug + once per seed), (b) after_write (repoops per feature, carries TRUE hidden outcome as confidence arg), (c) choose_action (maze, ONLY if uncertainty_planning active - so a maze mechanism must chain after UP and rewrite ctx["uncertainty_planning"]["ranked"]), (d) retrieve (selflab, ONLY if attention_budget active - unreachable, parked). => SelfLab is unreachable by new mechanisms this phase; Mechanism A targets RepoOps via after_write, Mechanism B targets Maze by refining UP's ranked frontier.
[2026-08-08 18:05:00] ARCHITECT: Mechanism A "residual_bias" (RepoOps). Hypothesis: evidence links store ONE noisy observation (gauss sigma 0.5 on true 0.1/0.7) and single-shot recall trusts the last write verbatim, so a good patch can lose to an overfit patch on a lucky noisy draw. memory_consolidation (parked) merges+reinforces globally WITHOUT using the ground truth available at write time; attention_budget (parked) caps the pool without de-noising. Mechanism: per-style EMA residual r[style] = observed - stored, learned in HOOK_after_write (env passes TRUE hidden outcome), and the just-written link confidence is rewritten to stored + r[style] (Kalman-style bias filter). Expected: RepoOps success_rate lifts (toward always picking good), no effect on Maze/SelfLab; compounds with UP by filling the one faculty the incumbent does not touch. Predicted domain: RepoOps. Predicted MoA: bias-correction sharpens prior separation between good/overfit/flaky.
[2026-08-08 18:05:00] ARCHITECT: Mechanism B "frontier_memory" (Maze). Hypothesis: uncertainty_planning is STATELESS across episodes of the same maze - it re-offers the same juicy pocket cell every episode even after it dead-ends. Maze runs 5 episodes per layout with fresh maps each episode, so only cross-episode memory can learn 'that cell is a dead end'. Honest progress signal available at choose_action time: minimum manhattan distance to goal reached while exploring. Mechanism: credit-assign each chosen target by the episode's best (smallest) goal-distance (REWARD -0.8 if <=4, PENALTY +1.0 otherwise), weights decay 0.5/episode, then re-rank UP's candidates score /= (1 + 0.10*weight[cell]) so proven-productive cells are nudged up and dead-ends nudged down. Genuine within-maze transfer (episodes share walls) that compounds with the IG score rather than replacing it. Cross-maze pollution bounded by per-cell identity + fast decay (documented imperfection). Predicted domain: Maze. Predicted MoA: adaptive exploration bonus / learned path caching across episodes.
